Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is the “ability to consummate” concept subject to Material Adverse Effect (MAE) carveouts?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: “Company Material Adverse Effect” means any event, circumstance, change, effect or occurrence (each, an “Effect”) that, individually or in the aggregate, has had or would reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the business, assets, liabilities, financial condition or results of operations of the Company and its Subsidiaries, taken as a whole, or would, or would reasonably be expected to, prevent, materially delay or materially impair the ability of the Company to consummate the transactions contemplated by this Agreement; provided, however, that with respect to the financial condition clause only, no Effect arising out of, resulting from, or related to any of the following shall be deemed to constitute a Company Material Adverse Effect or be taken into account in determining whether a Company Material Adverse Effect has occurred or would reasonably be expected to occur: (i) changes in global economic conditions or conditions in the financial, credit or securities markets; (ii) changes in political conditions or acts of war, terrorism, or other hostilities; (iii) changes in law or accounting principles; (iv) any natural disaster or other force majeure event; (v) the announcement or performance of this Agreement or the transactions contemplated hereby, including any impact on relationships with employees, customers, suppliers, or partners, except that this exclusion shall not apply to the ability to consummate the transactions; (vi) any failure to meet internal projections, forecasts, or estimates; (vii) any change in the Company’s stock price or trading volume, in and of itself; and (viii) any action taken by the Company that is required by this Agreement or with the written consent of the Parent. Effects arising from clauses (i) through (v) shall be considered in determining a Company Material Adverse Effect only if they have a disproportionate adverse impact on the Company relative to other industry participants, in which case only the incremental disproportionate impact shall be considered. (Pages 12-13)\nAnswer:
Choices:

